<h2>Multicountry Workshop on Enterprise Development and Development of Innovative Startup Business Ecosystems, 02 - 05 November 2026, Singapore (face to face), Self-Finance basis</h2>

<p>The National Productivity Organization (NPO), Ministry of Industries &amp; Production, Government of Pakistan, in collaboration with the Asian Productivity Organization (APO), Japan, is pleased to announce participation opportunities for Pakistani citizens through a competitive selection process for the following program on self-finance basis:</p>

<ol>
	<li><a href="https://npo.gov.pk/_apo_course/852/">26-SPP-SG-F1-01: <strong>Multicountry Workshop on Enterprise Development and Development of Innovative Startup Business Ecosystems</strong></a>, 02 - 05 November 2026, Singapore (Face to Face: Self Finance basis)<strong><u>NPO Deadline: 28<sup>th</sup> September 2026. </u></strong>(Kindly ignore the closing date mentioned in APO-Japan link) <strong>Note:</strong> APO Japan has requested that all applicants to fill their Biodata Form through Online Portal (previous APO Bio-data form in MS Excel format is not acceptable as per new APO policy)</li>
</ol>

<p>2. Ten (10) International participants from APO Member countries will take part in this program.<u> APO Secretariat, Japan will issue E-CERTIFICATE against full attendance</u>.</p>

<p>3. To download the <strong>Nomination Letter sample</strong> Please visit <a href="http://npo.gov.pk/apo/">http://npo.gov.pk/apo/</a>.</p>

<table>
	<tbody>
		<tr>
			<td>
			<p>Please fill Bio-Data Form online through APO Japan Portal URL: <a href="https://apo.my.site.com/s/programs">https://apo.my.site.com/s/programs</a>.</p>

			<p>(Click at code of program &gt; apply as participant &gt; enter country (Pakistan) &gt; enter email id &gt; enter code received at your email)</p>

			<p><strong>Following documents are also required for processing of nomination, and sent to email address: </strong><a><strong>sohaibnpopak@gmail.com</strong></a><strong> &amp; </strong><a><strong>faizan.npopak@gmail.com</strong></a></p>

			<ol>
				<li>CV on plain paper including date of birth, domicile (district &amp; province), education, experience, and details of foreign  trainings attended during the recent past.</li>
				<li>Copy of National Identity Card.</li>
				<li>Copy of the passport''s first page, with a minimum validity of eights months.</li>
				<li>Copy of domicile certificate.</li>
				<li>Nomination letter on NPO prescribed format, available on website (<a href="http://npo.gov.pk/apo/">http://npo.gov.pk/apo/</a>).</li>
				<li>Case processing fee: original scanned Fee payment receipt (Prerequisite), non-refundable upon withdrawal or dismissal.</li>
				<li>Sign the Undertaking on a PKR. 100/- (Rupees One Hundred only) stamp paper</li>
			</ol>
			</td>
		</tr>
	</tbody>
</table>

<p>4. Case of only shortlisted nominee’s will forward to APO, Japan for further evaluation. The final selection of nominee’s rests with the APO screening committee (not challengeable) subject to No financial liability on NPO Pakistan and APO Japan.</p>

<p>5. Processing Fee (Prerequisite) Non-refundable: PKR 4,000/- per applicant for Public Sector and PKR 6,000/- per applicant for Private Sector. Fee payment receipt in both cases either cash deposit in bank or online payment should be sent through email (bank details are available at NPO website).</p>

<p>6. In case of Selection participants from both the Public and Private Sectors will be responsible for bearing all kind of expenses related to their participation, including, International airfare, Boarding and lodging, Visa fee, Travel/medical insurance, PCR testing, Airport taxes, any other applicable charges/cancellation charges and any other personal or incidental expenses.</p>

<p>7. Visa is the responsibility of the selected candidate, we would also encourage any prospective applicant to check the applicable visa requirements and expected processing time at the earliest opportunity.</p>

<p>8. The incomplete and late nominations received after the above mentioned deadline will not be processed. Applicants fulfilling the prescribed criteria in respective APO Activity Notification may apply for the relevant program.</p>

<p>9. Kindly send nominations along with documents to <u>National Productivity Organization (NPO)</u>, APO Liaison Department, 11th Floor, Shaheed-e-Millat Secretariat, <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/Nazim-ud-Din+Road,+F-6%2F1,+Islamabad,+Pakistan?entry=gmail&amp;source=g">Nazim-ud-Din Road, F-6/1, Islamabad, Pakistan</a>.</p>

<p>10. For any inquiry and further information please contact Mr. Mohammad Sohiab, APO-LO on 051-9244254-5, 0332-5490277</p>

<p><strong>(M. Sohaib)</strong>      <br />
APO Liaison Department</p>

<p> </p>'
